BEHAVIOR map-init

DESCRIPTION
  Initializes an open-addressing (linear-probe) hash map in caller-owned
  memory: stores cap at offset 0 and clears every slot's used flag. Keys up to
  64 bytes, values up to 256 bytes; cap slots of 337 bytes each follow the
  header. Buffer must be at least map-buf-size(cap) bytes.

CONTRACT
  INPUT map bytes 262144
  INPUT cap int 8

HASH 54f37178

IMPLEMENTATION
  cv = LOAD cap 8
  STORE map cv 8 0
  i = 0
  LABEL loop
    d = IGE i cv 8
    BRANCH d done body
  LABEL body
    e = IMUL i 337 8
    off = IADD e 8 8
    STORE map 0 1 off
    i = IADD i 1 8
    JUMP loop
  LABEL done
END
